# PATENT CLAIM

## Claim 1

A cable bolt for reinforcing and stabilizing ground formations in geotechnical and mining applications, comprising:

a multi-strand cable structure defining a longitudinal axis and comprising:
- a central king wire extending along said longitudinal axis; and
- a plurality of outer wires, numbering between six and nine, helically wound around said central king wire at a lay length of between 150 mm and 300 mm, said outer wires and said central king wire being fabricated from a high-carbon steel alloy;

wherein said high-carbon steel alloy comprises, by weight percentage:
- carbon: 0.65% to 0.85%;
- manganese: 0.40% to 0.90%;
- silicon: 0.15% to 0.35%;
- chromium: 0.00% to 0.30%;
- sulfur: not more than 0.020%;
- phosphorus: not more than 0.020%;
- balance iron and incidental impurities;

wherein said high-carbon steel alloy exhibits a microstructure comprising tempered martensite and retained austenite, said retained austenite present in an amount of between 2% and 8% by volume as measured by X-ray diffraction analysis, said retained austenite being distributed substantially uniformly throughout said microstructure so as to impart increased ductility and resistance to hydrogen-induced cracking to said cable bolt;

a borehole anchoring mechanism disposed along at least a distal portion of said multi-strand cable structure, said anchoring mechanism comprising a plurality of deformations selected from the group consisting of bulges, nail-head profiles, indentations, and combinations thereof, formed integrally into said outer wires at spaced intervals along said distal portion, said deformations configured to mechanically key said cable bolt within a grout or resin annulus disposed in a borehole, thereby resisting axial pull-out under tensile load; and

a proximal end portion of said multi-strand cable structure configured to extend beyond said borehole and to receive a bearing plate and a fastening element for applying a pre-tensioning load to said cable bolt;

wherein said cable bolt exhibits an ultimate tensile strength of at least 250 kN and an elongation at failure of at least 3.5%.

## Claim 2

The cable bolt of claim 1, wherein said high-carbon steel alloy further comprises molybdenum in an amount of 0.05% to 0.25% by weight, and wherein said tempered martensite microstructure is produced by austenitizing said steel alloy at a temperature between 850°C and 950°C, followed by quenching and tempering at a temperature between 300°C and 450°C to stabilize said retained austenite.

## Claim 3

The cable bolt of claim 1, wherein said retained austenite is present in an amount of between 3% and 6% by volume.

## Claim 4

The cable bolt of claim 1, wherein said plurality of outer wires consists of eight wires wound around said central king wire in a single helical layer.

## Claim 5

The cable bolt of claim 1, wherein said borehole anchoring mechanism further comprises a plurality of birdcage sections formed by displacing said outer wires radially outward from said central king wire at discrete locations along said distal portion, said birdcage sections configured to enhance mechanical interlock with said grout or resin annulus.

## Claim 6

The cable bolt of claim 1, further comprising a corrosion-resistant coating disposed on an outer surface of said multi-strand cable structure, said coating selected from the group consisting of zinc, zinc-aluminum alloy, and epoxy-based polymer coatings.

## Claim 7

The cable bolt of claim 1, wherein said central king wire has a diameter greater than a diameter of each of said plurality of outer wires, such that said cable bolt has an overall nominal diameter of between 15 mm and 22 mm.

## Claim 8

The cable bolt of claim 1, wherein said deformations are formed by passing said outer wires through a series of shaped dies during a post-stranding deformation process, such that a spacing between adjacent deformations is between 150 mm and 400 mm.

## Claim 9

A method of reinforcing a ground formation, comprising:
inserting the cable bolt of claim 1 into a borehole formed in said ground formation;
introducing a grout or resin material into said borehole to encapsulate said distal portion of said cable bolt, thereby forming said grout or resin annulus in mechanical engagement with said borehole anchoring mechanism;
allowing said grout or resin material to cure; and
applying a pre-tensioning load to said proximal end portion of said cable bolt via said bearing plate and said fastening element.

